WEBVTT

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:48.950
Oh no!

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.910
It looks like the outdoor stage collapsed!

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.660
Seriously?

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.500
Collapsed?

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.410
This is a message from the Kao Council.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:02.120
Members of the Kao Council and
Ayanagi Festival committee members

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.290
please gather promptly in
the Ayanagi Hall meeting room.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:09.660
I repeat, members of the Kao Council
and Ayanagi Festival committee members...

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.000
The guys in charge are starting to act.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.750
So all we can do is wait
for their decision, huh?

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.450
Hoshitani!

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.870
No way...

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:41.580
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:48.700
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:56.540
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.040
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:04.580
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:12.830
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:19.120
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.160
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:27.620
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.330
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:37.080
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.330
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.750
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.290
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.790
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.870
This is an announcement from the Kao Council.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:02.580
"Act 12"

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:08.040
Due to the strong winds earlier,
the special outdoor stage has collapsed.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.700
Taking into consideration the
safety of the students and visitors,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:18.410
we are canceling all of the scheduled
performances on the outdoor stage.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.870
Canceling...

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.790
What the hell?

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:25.500
How can we not perform because
of a little wind and rain, you boor?!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:33.830
In addition, for the teams scheduled to do
their final performances on the outdoor stage,

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:40.000
there will be a make-up exam at a later date
in front of teachers and the Kao Council.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.450
He says we'll still do the
final round of performance exams.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.160
Just the exam part, anyway.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.700
But then...

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.040
...we can't show everyone our performance...

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.410
Hoshitani!

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.790
Please, let us perform!

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.870
Even if we were able to prepare another stage,

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:13.370
we would not be able to count
the performance for the exam.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.700
But--

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.500
The decision is final.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:22.330
Prioritizing everyone's safety is also
a responsibility of the Kao Council.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.000
No matter what kind of plant it is,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.830
if it's not planted in the ground,
it cannot bloom.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.040
Monsieur Otori.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.160
Long time no see.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.450
You haven't come to school since then.
What have you been up to all this time?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.370
I was running away. From those boys.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:59.580
Although, I seem to be so attached to them
that I want to help them the minute I see them.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.160
Otori, I do think the
current situation is unfortunate.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.200
However, there will be a make-up exam.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:11.870
The conditions will be better for them than
having to perform in this inclement weather.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.540
We will evaluate them fairly.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.200
<i>Oui</i> , of course.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.290
Those boys don't just want a make-up exam.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:30.200
We actors want an audience
to watch our best performances, right?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.120
Is it different for you guys?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:37.370
Those boys shine.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:43.410
Whether there's wind or rain,
they will not grow dim.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.370
Imagine--

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.160
The five of them standing on stage,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.580
the hems of their costumes
fluttering as they dance.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.660
There's a large audience in front of them.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.790
Applause and cheers
well up as the final curtain falls.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:07.450
I wanted to show them that sight...

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.790
How'd it go? What did Hiragi say?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:30.910
What about you guys?

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.330
All the stages are full...

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.580
And the Kao Council is
in charge of all the equipment.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.750
What should we do? Either way,
the Kao Council won't give us permission!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.660
Is the curtain falling before it even rises?

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.370
We can't give up. There must still be a way...

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:51.790
Hmm... What should we do?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.750
Who's there?

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.950
Inumine?!

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.410
Oh no! He heard us.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.700
Shall we?

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.120
Yeah.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.200
There you are.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.000
We were looking for you, Inumine.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.540
Oh, where were you guys?

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.660
When I looked around,
you were nowhere to be--

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.870
♪ Oh, ice cream! ♪

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:39.080
♪ Ice cream... ♪

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.080
I thought I told you not to eat anything cold

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.410
before the performance, Inu, you dog!

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:39.080
Sorry you had to see that.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:43.790
I heard your performance on the
outdoor stage was cancelled? Too bad!

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.160
Ugawa.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.700
It was inevitable with this storm.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.450
That was unfortunate.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.540
Don't talk about it in the past tense.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.870
It's not over yet.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.290
Yeah. We're not going
to give up until the very end.

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:00.580
Are you going to tell Hiragi...?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.750
I'm glad.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:09.040
Now we'll be able to focus
on our own performance.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.660
Thanks.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.660
Let's go, Inumine! House!

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.450
You have it hard, too, huh?

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:20.950
Right?

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:30.450
Well, it's fine to act defiant, but we won't
be able to do anything without a stage.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.910
Even if we have a stage,
if we push ahead with our performance,

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.450
we might end up getting punished.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:39.410
We're damned if we do,
and damned if we don't, huh?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.950
What would Otori do at a time like this?

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.000
We can have fun with this, boys.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.910
What was that?

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.660
I thought maybe...
that's what Otori would say...

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.870
It does sound like something he would say.
Even during a time like this.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.870
And he'd look really happy saying it.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.660
Yeah!

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.910
That's our great teacher for ya.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:11.250
Then let's be avant-garde till the end!

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:21.200
I just thought of something.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.790
What? A guerrilla performance?

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:40.500
If we use that spot, there's
a place for the audience to gather,

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.830
and if we set up the equipment
inside the school building,

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.330
then it won't be affected by
the rain or wind, right?

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.160
An outdoor stage in the middle of a storm, huh?

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.910
You're saying something crazy again.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.160
The performance programs are almost over.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.910
We might be able to borrow equipment now.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.410
I wonder if anyone will help us?

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.370
There's no use thinking about it.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:04.330
If it's between performing or not
performing, then there's only one answer.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.080
Please help us!

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.200
Sure.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:21.000
Thank you!

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:25.620
♪ We spread our arms... ♪

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.370
The equipment's set up.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:34.790
Thanks.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:35.660
What about over there?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:38.160
It's fine. The sound's back.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:44.830
What are you doing?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.700
Akatsuki, sir...

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.660
I'd heard that there were students
and staff running around

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.870
who weren't from the musical department.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.000
It was you guys, after all, huh?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:02.290
Please! Please let us perform!

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:06.500
I thought you were told that the
Kao Council canceled the performance?

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:09.000
If you go against us, you will be punished.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:15.870
Do you want to be washed away
in the storm with this performance?

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.080
This is stupid.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:26.700
Hurry up and take this down!

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.660
It's not stupid.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:35.620
What did you say?

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:40.410
There is no room for argument.
I said, take this down!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.620
What's that?

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:51.450
The Ayanagi Festival two years ago was
when I first saw the high schooler I admire.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.870
I wanted to stand on the same stage as him,

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:58.370
so it became my dream
to enter the musical department.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:02.330
But now I have a dream just as big.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:08.040
I want as many people as possible
to see our wonderful performance.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:13.660
That's our dream! That's Team Otori's musical!

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.790
That's why we will never give up.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.200
We...

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.750
...don't know how to give up on our dream.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.660
The rain...

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.500
We can make it if we go now!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.870
Yeah!

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.250
Are you guys planning
on defying the Kao Council?

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:52.290
You will not get away with this!

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.160
Excuse us.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.040
What are you doing? Hurry up and change!

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.250
Transform quickly.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.790
Team Otori's performance is about to begin!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.450
Team Otori's performance is about to begin!

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:31.410
The next performance is from Team Otori--

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.540
<i>Stardust Musical</i> !

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:44.580
Come on, everyone! It's time to play!

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:46.790
We're...

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.450
...stardust!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.950
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:04.250
Please excuse my want of eloquence,
but thank you for your presence on this day!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:09.120
Above all, I would ask of you--

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:13.160
This is too much trouble! No more greetings!

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:16.790
To each and every one
of you present here today--

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.750
Enjoy yourself until the end!

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:44.330
♪ Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams ♪

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:50.790
♪ On a night when you look up at a starless sky ♪

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:54.450
♪ Just remember (today) ♪

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:58.410
♪ The days we ran like crazy (together) ♪

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:02.750
♪ Those steps were miracles ♪

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:05.950
♪ Ring out, Countdown! ♪

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:09.620
♪ Taking off for the future from here ♪

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:13.540
♪ You will start singing again ♪

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.500
♪ There are things you lack ♪

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:20.540
♪ So you reach out desperately to grab them ♪

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:24.120
♪ These hot, passionate feelings overflowing ♪

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.700
♪ Make the light of the stars your ally ♪

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:31.370
♪ Even bluffing can become your pride ♪

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:35.000
♪ You can fly however you want ♪

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:41.000
♪ Everything starts now! ♪

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:56.040
♪ These steps have permeated my body ♪

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:59.370
♪ (Even if they're not perfect) ♪

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:04.910
♪ The more I worry,
the closer I get to my dream ♪

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.620
♪ (Get closer) ♪

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:12.580
♪ The boys who have grown wings sing ♪

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:17.200
♪ Those phrases were miracles ♪

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:20.290
♪ Ring out, Countdown! ♪

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:25.950
♪ Taking off for the future from here ♪

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:29.790
♪ You will start singing again ♪

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:33.040
♪ There are things you lack ♪

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:36.910
♪ So you reach out desperately to grab them ♪

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:40.330
♪ These hot, passionate feelings overflowing ♪

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:40.330
As expected of your students.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.830
They're just like you.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:44.080
♪ Make the light of the stars your ally ♪

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:47.790
No, they're doing <i>more</i> than I've taught them.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.790
♪ Even bluffing can become your pride ♪

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:51.500
♪ You can fly however you want ♪

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.370
The future is unknown.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:54.120
Their future, and ours.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.120
♪ These hot, passionate feelings ♪

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:58.660
♪ (I can't control this impulse) ♪

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:02.450
♪ Five stars shining (Dreams come true) ♪

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:08.540
♪ Everything starts now! ♪

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:29.660
Speaking of which, the person Hoshitani
said he admired... That was you, right?

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:34.330
It's out of character for me to be
the admired prince charming, though.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:38.370
You're right. The throne doesn't
need anyone but me on it.

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:42.120
However, it wouldn't be bad
to play with you sometimes, too.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.200
Otori, sir!

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:16.790
Japan's winters are so cold!

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:19.370
They're cold in France, too, aren't they?

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:21.120
Oh, there they are.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.540
Having fun, Akatsuki?

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.040
Mercy!

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.290
Mercy...

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.870
Snow? How elegant.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:55.200
Oh, it's beautiful!

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:58.950
We stars really are lucky!

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.700
Don't call yourself a star. It's embarrassing.

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.660
Come on, let's go cast away our earthly desires.

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.500
Later.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.500
Happy new year!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.540
Happy new year!

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.410
See you later!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.910
Shall we go, too?

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:40.950
You can't ride your motorcycle in the snow.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:42.870
Yeah, it's dangerous.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.330
Why don't you just ring in the new year here?

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.580
Huh?

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:51.790
Then maybe I will, too!

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.370
That sounds good!

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:58.620
Well, it wouldn't be too bad to slurp some
New Year's <i>soba</i> noodles with you guys.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.830
Don't talk about it. It's making me hungry.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.290
Well, I should go home.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.580
We're always busy visiting
people over the holiday.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:23.660
My mom's also been rushing me to get home
quickly because my brother's coming home.

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:28.660
My sisters are asking me to help
them line up for lucky grab bags.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:32.250
I'm going to go home
before the snow really sticks.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:36.660
Then I'll say goodbye here
since a car's coming to pick me up.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:38.540
I'm taking the bus.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:41.450
I'll catch a taxi on the street.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.950
I'm taking the train,
so it's the station for me.

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.700
I guess we should say goodbye here, then.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:50.290
Yeah, take care of yourselves.

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.330
Yeah, see you next year.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:53.620
See ya next year.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.910
Yeah, see you next year!

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.250
See you next year.

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:17.700
See you next year.

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:40.830
<i>The story starts from this place</i>

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:44.370
<i>I'm so excited, I can't help it</i>

00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:45.950
<i>We'll go over...</i>

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:47.500
<i>...the walls...</i>

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:49.910
<i>...in front of us</i>

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:54.910
<i>There were steps that we couldn't really do</i>

00:22:54.910 --> 00:22:58.450
<i>But I think they've gotten a little better</i>

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:01.160
<i>The work we've done when no one's looking...</i>

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:03.080
<i>...won't betray us</i>

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:05.160
<i>It definitely won't!</i>

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:08.830
